          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14. A city has two main roads which cross each other at the centre of the city. These two roads are along the North–South (N–S) direction and East–West (E–W) direction. All the other streets of the city run parallel to these roads and are 200 m apart. There are 10 streets in each direction."
            }
          ]
